To run the benchmarks, from within the benchmarks directory run:
   AR_VERSION=8.1 bundle exec ruby benchmark.rb [options]

AR_VERSION selects the ActiveRecord version, as it does for the test suite.
The database connection is read from test/database.yml, falling back to
test/database.default.yml (see the README for setting up the test databases).

The following options are supported:
  --adapter [String]   The database adapter to use. Defaults to mysql2.

  --do-not-delete       By default all records in the benchmark tables will be deleted at the end of the benchmark. This flag indicates not to delete the benchmark data.
  --num [Integer]      The number of objects to benchmark. This can be used multiple times. Defaults to 1000.
  --table-type [String]  The table type to test. This can be used multiple times. By default it is all table types.
  --to-csv [String]      Print results in a CSV file format
  --to-html [String]     Print results in HTML format (String filename must be supplied). This is the default, written to benchmark.html.

See "ruby benchmark.rb -h" for the complete listing of options.

EXAMPLES
--------
To output to html format:
  AR_VERSION=8.1 bundle exec ruby benchmark.rb --adapter=mysql2 --to-html=results.html

To output to csv format:
  AR_VERSION=8.1 bundle exec ruby benchmark.rb --adapter=mysql2 --to-csv=results.csv

LIMITATIONS
-----------
Currently MySQL is the only supported adapter to benchmark.

